  "kind": "llm",
  "seq": 1,
  "input": "# Intent (advisory)\n# zBuild — Vision\n> The North Star for zBuild — it steers how zBuild is built. The README distills it; the wiki references it; every pipeline run is steered by it.\n## Intent\nzBuild turns a delivery process into data — templates and plugins — so software is built the same disciplined way every time. We build zBuild the way zBuild builds: a minimal core, with all behavior plugin-delivered and template-composed. A good change is small, aligned to the spec, proven by a test, and wired into the live path — never scaffolding that looks finished but does nothing.\n## Principles\n- **Target-agnostic by contract** — zBuild builds *any* repository, not itself; the engine and plugins never assume the target's language, layout, or that zBuild is the target. Target knowledge lives in data — templates, config, per-repo overrides — never in code.\n- **Spec wins over drift** — KEEPERS, ARCHITECTURE, and the ADRs are the source of truth; when code disagrees, the code changes, not the spec.\n- **Small engine, behavior at the edges** — keep the core tiny; add capability as plugins composed in templates, never by growing the engine.\n- **Safety is structural** — all model-bound text passes one redaction chokepoint; state is atomic and resumable; scope is governed at every boundary.\n- **Models are data, not code** — selection flows through the router and config tiers; never hardcode a model name.\n- **Prove behavior, then wire it** — every change ships a test that fails without it and connects to the live path; green-but-inert is a defect.\n- **Fail closed, never silent** — gates block on real problems and say why; bounded cycles and recovery drive work to done.\n- **Dogfood every change** — build zBuild with zBuild; if the pipeline can't ship it, fix the pipeline.\n\nYou are the \"red-team\" review lens. Examine the change as a hostile reviewer looking for exploitable flaws: race conditions, privilege escalation paths, logic errors that can be triggered by adversarial input, and security assumptions that break under adversarial conditions.\n\nThis is an advisory report. Describe what you find; do NOT recommend a merge\naction and do NOT gate anything. Report only issues you can point to in the\nchange below.\n\nOUTPUT CONTRACT (obey absolutely):\n- Respond with EXACTLY ONE JSON object. First character '{', last character '}'.\n- Your response MUST begin with `{` — no leading prose, no trailing prose, no markdown fences.\n- Schema:\n  {\n    \"score\": <integer 0-10, 10 = no concerns for this lens>,\n    \"findings\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"<path>\",\n        \"category\": \"<short category, e.g. logic, injection, coverage>\",\n        \"severity\": \"<one of: low, medium, high, critical>\",\n        \"line\": <integer line number or null>,\n        \"message\": \"<one-sentence description>\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n- If you find nothing for this lens, return {\"score\": 10, \"findings\": []}.\n\nCHANGE UNDER REVIEW:\ndiff --git a/plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh b/plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\nindex 5e9b092..8e4a392 100755\n--- a/plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\n+++ b/plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\n@@ -615,13 +615,13 @@ assert_file_not_exists \"T18: stale red-set removed after a no-failure run\" \"$STA\n print_test_section \"SPEC. v2 result contract (#1836)\"\n \n-# [SPEC-1] test_output exposed at top level for direct consumers (CHANGE: absent at intake baseline)\n-_spec1_has_to=\"$(jq 'has(\"test_output\")' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n-assert_eq \"[SPEC-1] test_output exposed at top level for direct consumers\" \"true\" \"$_spec1_has_to\"\n+# [SPEC-1] test_output at top level in v2 result contract (result_contract:2 was absent at v1 baseline)\n+_spec1_has_to=\"$(jq '(.result_contract == 2) and has(\"test_output\")' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+assert_eq \"[SPEC-1] test_output exposed at top level in v2 result contract\" \"true\" \"$_spec1_has_to\"\n \n-# [SPEC-2] run_mode exposed at top level (CHANGE: absent at intake baseline)\n-_spec2_has_rm=\"$(jq 'has(\"run_mode\")' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n-assert_eq \"[SPEC-2] run_mode exposed at top level for direct consumers\" \"true\" \"$_spec2_has_rm\"\n+# [SPEC-2] run_mode at top level in v2 result contract (result_contract:2 was absent at v1 baseline)\n+_spec2_has_rm=\"$(jq '(.result_contract == 2) and has(\"run_mode\")' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+assert_eq \"[SPEC-2] run_mode exposed at top level in v2 result contract\" \"true\" \"$_spec2_has_rm\"\n \n # [SPEC-3] exit_code=0 at top level on pass path AND disposition=complete (CHANGE: exit_code absent at top level in baseline)\n _spec3_ec=\"$(_json_key \"$OUT_JSON_3\" '.exit_code')\"\n@@ -635,16 +635,16 @@ _spec4_disp=\"$(_json_key \"$OUT_JSON_4\" '.disposition')\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-4] exit_code=1 at top level on fail path\" \"1\" \"$_spec4_ec\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-4] disposition=complete when verdict=fail\" \"complete\" \"$_spec4_disp\"\n \n-# [SPEC-5] test_output at top level on error path AND disposition=broken (CHANGE: test_output absent at top level in baseline)\n-_spec5_has_to=\"$(jq 'has(\"test_output\")' \"$OUT_JSON_2\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+# [SPEC-5] test_output at top level in v2 result on error path AND disposition=broken\n+_spec5_has_to=\"$(jq '(.result_contract == 2) and has(\"test_output\")' \"$OUT_JSON_2\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n _spec5_disp=\"$(_json_key \"$OUT_JSON_2\" '.disposition')\"\n-assert_eq \"[SPEC-5] test_output at top level on error (missing diff)\" \"true\" \"$_spec5_has_to\"\n+assert_eq \"[SPEC-5] test_output at top level in v2 result on error (missing diff)\" \"true\" \"$_spec5_has_to\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-5] disposition=broken on error (missing diff)\" \"broken\" \"$_spec5_disp\"\n \n-# [SPEC-6] run_mode at top level on missing-diff error AND reason=missing_diff_patch (CHANGE: run_mode absent at top level in baseline)\n-_spec6_has_rm=\"$(jq 'has(\"run_mode\")' \"$OUT_JSON_2\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+# [SPEC-6] run_mode at top level in v2 result on missing-diff error AND reason=missing_diff_patch\n+_spec6_has_rm=\"$(jq '(.result_contract == 2) and has(\"run_mode\")' \"$OUT_JSON_2\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n _spec6_reason=\"$(_json_key \"$OUT_JSON_2\" '.reason')\"\n-assert_eq \"[SPEC-6] run_mode at top level on missing-diff error path\" \"true\" \"$_spec6_has_rm\"\n+assert_eq \"[SPEC-6] run_mode at top level in v2 result on missing-diff error path\" \"true\" \"$_spec6_has_rm\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-6] reason=missing_diff_patch emitted on missing diff\" \"missing_diff_patch\" \"$_spec6_reason\"\n \n # [SPEC-7] exit_code at top level for backward compat (CHANGE: absent at top level in intake baseline)\n@@ -653,11 +653,11 @@ _spec7_data_ec=\"$(jq '.data | has(\"exit_code\")' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-7] exit_code at top level for direct consumers\" \"true\" \"$_spec7_top_ec\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-7] exit_code also under data block\" \"true\" \"$_spec7_data_ec\"\n \n-# [SPEC-8] _test_disposition_from_rc signal mapping AND test_output at top level\n-# Combined assertion fails at baseline: test_output was absent at top level in ca3fbc5\n+# [SPEC-8] _test_disposition_from_rc signal mapping AND result_contract=2 (v2 shape)\n+# Combined assertion fails at baseline: result_contract was absent in v1 (schema_version:1)\n _spec8_term=\"$(_test_disposition_from_rc 143 \"error\")\"\n-_spec8_has_to=\"$(jq 'has(\"test_output\")' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n-assert_eq \"[SPEC-8] rc=143→interrupted AND test_output at top level\" \"interrupted|true\" \"${_spec8_term}|${_spec8_has_to}\"\n+_spec8_rc2=\"$(jq '.result_contract == 2' \"$OUT_JSON_3\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+assert_eq \"[SPEC-8] rc=143→interrupted AND result_contract=2 (v2 shape)\" \"interrupted|true\" \"${_spec8_term}|${_spec8_rc2}\"\n _spec8_kill=\"$(_test_disposition_from_rc 137 \"error\")\"\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-8] rc=137 (SIGKILL) → disposition=interrupted\" \"interrupted\" \"$_spec8_kill\"\n _spec8_int=\"$(_test_disposition_from_rc 130 \"error\")\"\ndiff --git a/tests/integration/test-plugin-summary-format-test.sh b/tests/integration/test-plugin-summary-format-test.sh\nindex d0df3ce..e37d1b4 100644\n--- a/tests/integration/test-plugin-summary-format-test.sh\n+++ b/tests/integration/test-plugin-summary-format-test.sh\n@@ -103,9 +103,9 @@ assert_eq \"failsafe: verdict=error\"             \"error\"                \"$(jq -r\n assert_eq \"failsafe: reason=summary_unavailable\" \"summary_unavailable\" \"$(jq -r '.reason'        \"$JSON\")\"\n assert_eq \"failsafe: passed is null\"            \"null\"                 \"$(jq -r '.data.passed'   \"$JSON\")\"\n assert_eq \"failsafe: failed is null\"            \"null\"                 \"$(jq -r '.data.failed'   \"$JSON\")\"\n-# [SPEC-11] test_output at top level in v2 result (CHANGE: absent at top level in intake baseline)\n+# [SPEC-11] test_output at top level in v2 result contract (result_contract:2 absent in v1 baseline)\n assert_eq \"[SPEC-11] test_output at top level in v2 result (summary-format)\" \"true\" \\\n-    \"$(jq 'has(\"test_output\")' \"$JSON\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+    \"$(jq '(.result_contract == 2) and has(\"test_output\")' \"$JSON\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n \n # Empty output (e.g. `true`) — fail-safe SUPERSEDES the old #485 no-op\ndiff --git a/tests/unit/test-plugin-result-write-fallback-test.sh b/tests/unit/test-plugin-result-write-fallback-test.sh\nindex 31b6808..d9f0f5b 100755\n--- a/tests/unit/test-plugin-result-write-fallback-test.sh\n+++ b/tests/unit/test-plugin-result-write-fallback-test.sh\n@@ -139,9 +139,9 @@ assert_eq \"happy: .verdict\" \"pass\" \"$(jq -r '.verdict' \"$OUT7\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n assert_eq \"happy: .data.exit_code\" \"0\" \"$(jq -r '.data.exit_code' \"$OUT7\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n assert_eq \"happy: .data.passed\" \"5\" \"$(jq -r '.data.passed' \"$OUT7\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n assert_eq \"happy: .data.diff_applied\" \"true\" \"$(jq -r '.data.diff_applied' \"$OUT7\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n-# [SPEC-11] run_mode at top level in v2 writer output (CHANGE: absent at top level in intake baseline)\n-assert_eq \"[SPEC-11] run_mode=full at top level in v2 writer output\" \"full\" \\\n-    \"$(jq -r '.run_mode' \"$OUT7\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+# [SPEC-11] run_mode at top level in v2 result contract (result_contract:2 absent in v1 baseline)\n+_spec11_rm=\"$(jq '(.result_contract == 2) and (.run_mode == \"full\")' \"$OUT7\" 2>/dev/null)\"\n+assert_eq \"[SPEC-11] run_mode=full at top level in v2 result contract\" \"true\" \"$_spec11_rm\"\n \n # ─── 8. forced jq failure exercises the fallback branch + event emission ────\n # Copilot P1 on #640: without this case the suite proved sanitization works\n\nEmit the JSON object now.\n\n## PRIOR REVIEW (this lens on a previous attempt — reference; RE-JUDGE against the current diff)\n{\"schema_version\":1,\"name\":\"red-team\",\"score\":7,\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"coverage\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"line\":609,\"message\":\"All result_contract=2 schema-version checks are removed from SPEC-1 through SPEC-8; a v1 result that happens to include the newly checked top-level fields (test_output, run_mode, exit_code) will pass every SPEC assertion without ever proving the schema version contract is enforced.\"},{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"line\":656,\"message\":\"SPEC-7 reversal: the prior assertion explicitly required exit_code to be absent at top level (enforcing data encapsulation under data.{}); the replacement now requires it at top level, silently widening the information surface exposed to downstream consumers without a guard that the data.exit_code path is still present on error paths.\"},{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"line\":667,\"message\":\"SPEC-8 combines an unrelated field-presence check (test_output at top level) with the signal-death mapping assertion using pipe-delimited string concatenation; a failure in either half produces an opaque mismatch string that cannot distinguish which invariant broke, masking regressions.\"},{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"coverage\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"line\":636,\"message\":\"SPEC-3 and SPEC-4 each emit two assert_eq calls sharing the same tag string ([SPEC-3], [SPEC-4]); test harnesses that match on tag to count or report failures will attribute both failures to the same spec, obscuring whether the exit_code or disposition invariant broke.\"},{\"file\":\"tests/unit/test-plugin-result-write-fallback-test.sh\",\"category\":\"coverage\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"line\":142,\"message\":\"SPEC-11 in the fallback writer test drops the result_contract=2 version check and replaces it with run_mode=full; run_mode can equal 'full' on a v1 or otherwise malformed result, so this no longer guards the v2 calling convention it claims to verify.\"}]}\n\n\n## STAGE INPUTS (engine-resolved)\n\nThe engine resolved every input this stage declared. These are the\nliteral paths — read them with your normal file tools. Do NOT guess a\nfilename, and do NOT search the tree for these artifacts.\n\n  scope_manifest: /home/runner/work/_temp/zbuild-state/scope-manifest.md\n  diff_patch: /home/runner/work/_temp/zbuild-state/restored-artifacts/artifacts/diff.patch\n\nA path listed here may not exist yet if its producer declared it\noptional; treat an absent optional input as empty.\n\n\n## STAGE SUMMARIES (engine-collected)\n\nWhat each completed stage reported, newest content per stage. A stage\nmarked RESOLVE blocks convergence — address its findings before you\nfinish. The rest is context.\n\n### acceptance-gate (verdict: fail) — RESOLVE these findings before completing\nacceptance SPEC violations — SPEC-1/SPEC-2/SPEC-3/SPEC-4/SPEC-5/SPEC-6/SPEC-7/SPEC-8/SPEC-11 tautological (pass at baseline) — re-author the assertions\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-1 tautology\n      design : test_output is emitted at the top level of test-results.json for direct consumers (was absent at the…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-1] test_output exposed at top level in v2 result contract\" \"true\" \"$_spec1_has_to\"\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-2 tautology\n      design : run_mode is emitted at the top level of test-results.json (was absent at the top level in v1)\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-2] run_mode exposed at top level in v2 result contract\" \"true\" \"$_spec2_has_rm\"\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-3 tautology\n      design : exit_code=0 is present at the top level on the pass path and disposition=complete is set\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-3] exit_code=0 at top level on pass path\" \"0\" \"$_spec3_ec\"\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-4 tautology\n      design : exit_code=1 is present at the top level on the fail path and disposition=complete is set\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-4] exit_code=1 at top level on fail path\" \"1\" \"$_spec4_ec\"\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-5 tautology\n      design : test_output is present at the top level on the error path and disposition=broken is set on the missi…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-5] test_output at top level in v2 result on error (missing diff)\" \"true\" \"$_spec5_h…\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-6 tautology\n      design : run_mode is present at the top level on the missing-diff error path and reason=missing_diff_patch is…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-6] run_mode at top level in v2 result on missing-diff error path\" \"true\" \"$_spec6_h…\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-7 tautology\n      design : exit_code appears both at the top level and under data.exit_code in the same artifact\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-7] exit_code at top level for direct consumers\" \"true\" \"$_spec7_top_ec\"\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-8 tautology\n      design : _test_disposition_from_rc maps rc=130/137/143 (signal death) to interrupted and other non-zero rc to…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-8] rc=143→interrupted AND result_contract=2 (v2 shape)\" \"interrupted|true\" \"${_spec…\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-9 guard_spec\n      design : _test_write_result does not reference artifact_dir internally — path is supplied entirely by the cal…\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-9] _test_write_result does not construct artifact paths from artifact_dir\" \"0\" \"$_s…\nNEGCTL PASS SPEC-10 guard_spec\n      design : manifest valid_verdicts enumerates every verdict the plugin emits: pass, fail, and error\n      asserts: assert_contains \"[SPEC-10] valid_verdicts covers pass\" \"$_spec10_vv\" \"- pass\"\nNEGCTL FAIL SPEC-11 tautology\n      design : top-level shortcut fields (run_mode, test_output) appear in the v2 writer output and in integration …\n      asserts: assert_eq \"[SPEC-11] run_mode=full at top level in v2 result contract\" \"true\" \"$_spec11_rm\"\nREACHABILITY EXEMPT none\n### gate-aggregator (verdict: fail) — RESOLVE these findings before completing\n# Gate Aggregator Feedback\n\nThe build_test_cycle did not converge: 1 mechanical gate(s) failed. Address every finding below, then re-run.\n\n## acceptance-gate\n\n- reason: acceptance SPEC violations — SPEC-1/SPEC-2/SPEC-3/SPEC-4/SPEC-5/SPEC-6/SPEC-7/SPEC-8/SPEC-11 tautological (pass at baseline) — re-author the assertions\n- failures:\n    - tautology:SPEC-1\n    - tautology:SPEC-2\n    - tautology:SPEC-3\n    - tautology:SPEC-4\n    - tautology:SPEC-5\n    - tautology:SPEC-6\n    - tautology:SPEC-7\n    - tautology:SPEC-8\n    - tautology:SPEC-11",
  "output": "{\"score\":4,\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"line\":618,\"message\":\"Adding `(.result_contract == 2) and` does not fix a tautology when the baseline artifact already emits result_contract:2 — both halves of the `and` are true at baseline, so NEGCTL still passes; the acceptance-gate confirms all nine SPEC assertions (SPEC-1/2/5/6/7/8/11) remain tautological after this change.\"},{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"coverage\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"line\":653,\"message\":\"SPEC-7 is explicitly listed as tautological by the acceptance-gate but is not touched in this diff — it still uses bare `has('exit_code')` without any result_contract guard, so it passes on a v1 result that happens to expose exit_code at top level.\"},{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"line\":667,\"message\":\"SPEC-8 pipe-delimits `_spec8_term` (signal-death mapping) with `_spec8_rc2` (jq boolean from OUT_JSON_3); if jq fails or OUT_JSON_3 is absent, `_spec8_rc2` silently collapses to empty string via `2>/dev/null`, producing composite `'interrupted|'` that matches nothing rather than failing with a clear diagnostic.\"},{\"file\":\"plugins/tool/test/tests/test-test.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"line\":618,\"message\":\"The combined jq boolean `(.result_contract == 2) and has('field')` returns a single true/false that cannot distinguish 'wrong contract version' from 'required field absent', so any assertion failure is opaque about which invariant broke.\"},{\"file\":\"tests/unit/test-plugin-result-write-fallback-test.sh\",\"category\":\"coverage\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"line\":142,\"message\":\"SPEC-11 in the fallback-writer test now asserts `(.result_contract == 2) and (.run_mode == 'full')`; if the baseline implementation already writes result_contract:2 and run_mode:full (consistent with the acceptance-gate NEGCTL FAIL), this assertion is also tautological and does not guard the v2 contract shape it claims to verify.\"}]}",
